welcome our animation bronze medal  winner undress Saul off receiving this  award is a tremendous honor and I'm very  grateful to be here with all these great  films and I'd like to thank the academy  for this amazing honor and just this  week that we've had these meetings and  whatnot that have been so inspiring and  really just inspired me to move forward  and keep doing creative work in my  career and there's no way I could have  ever made this film without my amazing  girlfriend sun-hi Yoon who did the  special effects and colored over half of  it and also put up with me bouncing  ideas off of her for months and that  deserves an applause oh also my amazing  composer Cal Blanton Ross who did an  amazing job with the score and with  sound design Hagen I'd like to thank my  mom and dad Peter and Sylvia salif who  are here tonight as well and they've  always encouraged me and supported me  usually for the most part whatever I  wanted to do as well as my brother  Carlos and sister-in-law Jen who have  always been there for me and there to  give me feedback and all that great  stuff so the calarts character animation  department really I feel nurtured our  exploration and trying to find our own  visions and I'd like to thank David and  Jennifer skelly who were my story  teachers and without that class the film  would have never been fleshed out the  way the story would have never turned  out the way it did so I'd like to thank  them for that and then I'd like to thank  the great corny Cole and my animation  teacher Ted tea and Kevin Johnson as  well as my mentor Mike wing I'd also  like to thank Derek Diana Ethan and  Carly who did additional coloring on it  and I'd also like to thank God for  are being on this path of making  animated films that I hope are and will  continue to be inspiring and just fun to  watch for everybody so thank you all  very much
 

